---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import StepsStrip from '../components/StepsStrip.astro';

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'What are a PDF\'s stored details?',
    a: 'Every PDF carries a small label card inside the file: a title, an author, sometimes a subject, keywords, the program that made it, and the dates it was made and last changed. Readers and search tools show these (a PDF viewer\'s properties panel reads the same card), and they travel with the file wherever it goes.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does wiping the details clean my document?',
    a: 'No, and this page will not pretend otherwise. Wiping removes the label card only. The pages, their words and pictures, hidden layers and everything else inside the file stay exactly as they were. If a page itself shows something it should not, that is an editing job on the page, not a details job.',
  },
  {
    q: 'I wiped the card. Why does the file still show a title somewhere?',
    a: 'Some files carry a second copy of the details in what is called an XMP block, which some programs read instead of the card. This page checks for one, says so in the table when a file has one, and the wipe takes it too.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why are the dates written so strangely?',
    a: 'Dates are stored in the file\'s own format: D: then year, month, day, hour, minute, second. The table shows that stored form first, exactly as the file carries it, and next to it the same date read out in plain words (15 January 2025, 10:30:00), taken from the stored digits with no timezone conversion, so the reading can never drift from what the file says.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where does my document go?',
    a: 'Nowhere. It is read into this page and its details are read and written in your browser. Watch the network panel while it works if you want to check.',
  },
];
const faqJson = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faq.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
});
const howToJson = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'HowTo',
  name: "How to view, change or wipe a PDF's stored details",
  step: [
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 1, name: "Pick the PDF", text: "Drop a PDF on the tray, or click to pick one. It stays on this device. Its stored details are read and shown before anything can be changed." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 2, name: "Read the label card", text: "The table shows every stored line exactly as the file carries it, including 'not set' for the lines the file leaves blank." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 3, name: "Change it or wipe it", text: "Type a new title or author and save (leave a box empty to clear that line), or wipe the whole card, including the XMP second copy when the file carries one." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 4, name: "Download the finished PDF", text: "Take the finished file away. The table then shows the finished file's details, read back from the file itself." },
  ],
});
---

<Base title="PDF metadata: see, change or wipe the details stored in a PDF, free · Benchzy" description="See the details a PDF stores about itself (title, author, dates, maker), change the title or author, or wipe the whole label card, inside your browser. Nothing is uploaded.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4">
    <section class="mt-8">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-accent-deep">PDF tools · the label card</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-black mt-2">A PDF's stored details</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        Every PDF carries a small label card inside the file: title, author, dates, the
        program that made it. The label card is the same record your PDF viewer's
        Properties panel shows (in some viewers it is under File, then Properties). See
        yours exactly as stored, fix the title or author, or wipe the whole card before
        the file goes out. Everything runs in your browser; the document is never uploaded.
      </p>
    </section>

    <StepsStrip who="For checking what a file says about itself before you send it on, fixing a wrong title on a report, or wiping the label card from a file you are about to publish." steps={[{ n: '01', t: 'Pick the PDF' }, { n: '02', t: 'Read its stored details' }, { n: '03', t: 'Change or wipe, then download' }]} />

    <section class="ticket mt-6 p-5 sm:p-7" id="md-tool">
      <div id="md-tray" class="tray p-6 text-center cursor-pointer" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Pick a PDF">
        <p class="font-display text-xl font-bold">Drop a PDF on the tray, or click to pick one</p>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-soft mt-2">PDF · it stays on this device</p>
        <input id="md-file" type="file" accept="application/pdf,.pdf" class="hidden" />
      </div>
      <p class="file-loaded hidden" data-loaded-for="md-file" role="status"></p>

      <div class="grid gap-6 mt-6 md:grid-cols-[1fr_320px]">
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">The label card, as stored</h2>
          <dl id="md-view" class="mt-2">
            <div class="spec-row"><dt>details</dt><dd>no file picked yet</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft mt-6">Change the title or author</h2>
          <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
            <label class="grid gap-1">
              <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">Title</span>
              <input id="md-title" type="text" class="border border-ink bg-ticket px-3 py-2" autocomplete="off" />
            </label>
            <label class="grid gap-1">
              <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">Author</span>
              <input id="md-author" type="text" class="border border-ink bg-ticket px-3 py-2" autocomplete="off" />
            </label>
            <p class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-soft">Leave a box empty to clear that line.</p>
            <button id="md-save" class="btn-primary" type="button" disabled>Save the label card</button>
            <button id="md-strip" class="btn-ghost" type="button" disabled>Wipe the whole card</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">File spec</h2>
          <dl id="md-spec" class="mt-2">
            <div class="spec-row"><dt>file</dt><dd>none picked yet</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="action-note">
            This tool changes the file's label card, not its contents. Wiping the card is
            not cleaning the document; the honest limits below say exactly what stays.
          </p>
          <p id="md-status" class="font-mono text-sm mt-4 leading-relaxed" aria-live="polite">Pick a PDF to begin.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="md-result" class="receipt hidden mt-8">
        <div class="tear pt-5 flex items-center gap-4 flex-wrap">
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold">Result</h2>
          <span class="stamp" id="md-stamp">Done on your device</span>
        </div>
        <p id="md-achieved" class="mt-3 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl"></p>
        <a id="md-download" class="btn-primary inline-block no-underline mt-3" href="#" download>Download the PDF</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">How it works</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The details live in a small record inside the file, separate from the pages. This
          page reads that record and shows every line exactly as stored, blanks included.
          Dates are shown in the file's own stored format (D: then year, month, day, hour,
          minute, second) with the same date read out in plain words beside it. Some files also carry a second copy in an XMP block; when a file has
          one, the table says so, and the wipe removes it as well. Saving writes only the
          record: this page never stamps its own name or today's date into your file's
          card. The download is how we protect your privacy: the program that does this
          job is part of this page, loaded from this site, and your file is read into the
          page and never uploaded. After a change, the table is read back from the
          finished file, so what it shows is the file's own state, not the plan.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Honest limits</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Wiping these details is not the same as cleaning a document. It removes the label
          card only: the pages, their words and pictures, hidden layers, earlier workings
          kept inside the content, and anything written on a page itself (a name typed in
          the text, a logo, a footer) all stay exactly as they were. Removing a name from
          the card does not remove it from the pages. If a page shows something it should
          not, that is an editing job on the page itself; no tool here paints over page
          content and calls it removed.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">A password-protected PDF keeps its details behind the password. Take the password off first with the <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/unlock-pdf/">unlock tool</a>, then bring the file back.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 mb-4">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4">
        {faq.map((f) => (
          <article class="ticket-soft p-5">
            <h3 class="font-bold">{f.q}</h3>
            <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed mt-1">{f.a}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqJson}></script>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={howToJson}></script>
  <script>
    import '../scripts/pdf-metadata.js';
  </script>
</Base>
